    1. Pick grid dims in [13-19] x [12-22], and 1-3 template shapes (distinct from {h-bar, v-bar, plus, X}).
    2. Assign each template a unique (center_color, shell_color) pair from non-zero colors; center and shell sets disjoint.
    3. For each template, decide 1-3 partial copies (mix of center-only and shell-only; at least 1 shell-only across all templates).
    4. Place all completed motifs (1 template + its partials) on the grid with Chebyshev bbox gap >= 2. Each motif center must allow full shape in-bounds (margin >= 1).
    5. Record the output grid (all motifs complete).
    6. Derive input by removing shell pixels from center-only partials and removing center pixel from shell-only partials. Templates stay complete.
